note("TURBOCHARGER SPEED CHAIN SETTLED (code + e2m + DTC): fuel_demand_quantity (0x40afe6) is the turbocharger speed in KRPM x 0.008, not a fuel quantity. Chain: TPU-B channel 1 (function 0xd period measurement, like the vehicle speed sensor on TPU-B 2) -> cm848_turbochargerSpeedSensorInterruptHandler -> cm848_updateTurbochargerSpeedSensor (frequency, Hz) -> table to speed, two rate limiters, filter, peak hold (cm848_calculateTurbochargerSpeedSensorValue) = turbocharger_speed_sensor_value (e2m Turbo_Speed_Sensor); in parallel cm848_estimateTurbochargerSpeed (was cm848_processProtectionEntry) = turbocharger_speed_estimate (e2m Turbo_Speed_Est, from charge pressure, engine speed and a 3-D table); cm848_selectTurbochargerSpeedSource picks sensor / estimate / global default (turbocharger_speed_source 0 / 1 / 2, e2m Turbo_Speed_Source) into turbocharger_speed. The input is a TPU timer channel, not a generic QADC sensor channel: the e2m lists its result in the generic sensor block (Turbo_Speed_Sensor 0x01196644 / Turbo_Speed_Default 0x01196646), which is the RAM pair 0x40bdc4 / 0x40bdc6 at the generic block offsets (base 0x40bd80), but only the TPU code writes that pair (the QADC channel 29 wrapper sensorChannelTypeB_*_axis3 uses 0x40bdd8 / 0x40bdda). ON THIS TRUCK the sensor is not installed (0x3ff71a Turbo_Speed_Sensor_Installed = 0, signal mode 0x100, frequency 0, period 0xffffffff in the dump; docs/ecu_pinout.md has no turbo speed pin), so turbocharger_speed is the ESTIMATE (source 1, 2086 = 16.7 KRPM at engine off). DTCs (ROM 0x5985a fault -> slot, obd_dtc_code_table 0x5b57c slot -> code, computed from the ROM image): fault 611 (bit 3 of fault_detected_bits_608_to_623) = P2581, fault 613 (bit 5) = P2580, fault 618 (bit 10) = P2579; faults 619 / 620 = B1934 (raw 0x9934; the DTC letter is the top two bits of the table word, verified: it reproduces word 32 = B1971-B1976 of task 027) with no named setter in the turbo speed code. By SAE J2012 (from memory, not in the repo) P2579 / P2580 / P2581 are the turbocharger / supercharger speed sensor A circuit range-performance / low / high codes, which fits the code: 611 = frequency above the high limit, 613 = below the low limit (engine running, boost present), 618 = rate of change out of range. E2M NAMES: the whole module is e2m Turbo_Speed_* / TSE_* / TPE_* (state 0x0117C800, 0x0118CB00, 0x011A3500; cal 0x0117CA00); the three source / state words are Turbo_Speed_Source, Turbo_Speed_State, Turbo_Speed_IR_State, Turbo_Speed_Disabled.")
note("TURBOCHARGER SPEED, OTHER CONSUMERS (names not changed here): cm848_calculateBoostTorqueOffset (0x13294) = the e2m 'charge pressure estimate with turbo speed sensor' (Charge_Press_Est_With_TSS / _EStat_With_TSS, status 0x80 / 0x40, thresholds boost_control_fuel_lower_threshold_cal / boost_control_fuel_upper_threshold_cal = C_Charge_Press_Turbo_Low / High_Thd); governor_adjustment_compare (0x5043b4) compares turbocharger_speed with an altitude-dependent threshold (governor_adjustment_fuel_qty_threshold is a turbocharger speed threshold, governor_adjustment_boost_threshold is compared with exhaust_metal_temperature at 0x40a68a); cm848_calculateWastegateDutyRequest uses charge_flow_turbocharger_speed_derate_limit - turbocharger_speed as its first error term; cm848_estimateCompressorOutletTemperature uses turbocharger_speed x 0x106 / 10000 / temperature factor as the corrected speed. The comments of every row that quotes fuel_demand_quantity / boost_control_mode / fuel_smoke_limit_mode / governor_speed_reference_raw / governor_temperature_correction / egr_fuel_pressure_ratio / egr_smoke_limit_* / throttle_rate_filter_reset_flag need the refresh step after this file is applied (the 24 calibration rows and the five charge_flow_turbocharger_speed_derate_* rows already say 'the variable's own rename is left as a lead').")
